<title>FRANCE: Jospin says health spending controls essential.</title>
<headline>Jospin says health spending controls essential.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Lionel Jospin said on Thursday that France had both to improve the health system and control spending.</p>
<p>He told parliament in a keynote speech that future goals would be fixed in early 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;Access to health, to learning and to justice must be guaranteed...Universal health insurance will be put in place,&quot; Jospin said. &quot;Control of health spending is essential. But for the future, we must adapt the current framework.&quot;</p>
<p>A national health conference in early 1998 would allow France to &quot;redefine objectives and resources&quot;, he said.</p>
</text>
